                  commands: "# RESULTS.md\n\n## Setup\nModel, CHAOS_RATE, TRIALS, date run.\n\n## Results\n(paste both tables from compare.py)\n\n## What each change fixed\n| Change | Failure cause it targeted | Evidence (task, trace file) |\n|---|---|---|\n| retry with backoff | | |\n| empty-result re-check | | |\n| output check (BadOutput) | | |\n| schema in error message | | |\n| system prompt: say what is missing | | |\n| graceful finish | | |\n\n## What still fails, and why\n\n## What hardening cost\nTokens and seconds per run, before vs. after.\n\n\n# then, in the terminal:\ngit add .\ngit status --short\ngit commit -m \"Lab 4 - fault injection, hardening, before/after results\"",
                  expect: "The staged list includes chaos.py, tasks.py, eval_run.py, compare.py, check_chaos.py, check_hardening.py, the hardened tools.py and agent.py, results/clean.json, results/before.json, results/after.json, traces/eval/ and RESULTS.md — and neither .env nor data/town.db. Add your AI-LOG.md row first.",
                  point: "\"Hardening helped\" is a claim; the change-to-cause table is the evidence. Some changes will turn out to have done nothing — say so. Knowing which defence actually earned its keep is the engineering judgement this lab is grading.",
